10	
11	On 2026-11-04 Kenneth rejected a two-part printer status (reachability plus activity) as over-engineered: "Let's do just one status… users can intuitively understand." He also said busy and printing are the same to users, and that a not-connected card needs a way to tell whether that is expected (powered off) or to troubleshoot.
12	
13	Proposed single list (not yet agreed): Not connected (reason + "Last connected …" + Reconnect), Ready (with "last print finished/failed" only when the printer says), Printing (includes heating, homing for a job), Paused, Needs attention (printer's message), Connected (reachable, activity not reported), Connecting… (only before the first answer). Klipper shut down / "Lost communication with MCU" maps to Not connected with Klipper's message.
14	
15	Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ version 1793859430-86aa, Main Page, row at y=2960 under the title "Printer card · one status (proposal, 2026-11-04)": `printer-status-01`…`05` (three Home screens, five-printer full vs short-rows comparison, every-status sheet). Kenneth had the camera put back (2026-11-05): 135 px LIVE block on Printing and Paused cards (Bambu, and Klipper when Moonraker lists a webcam). With it the printing card is 412 px vs 265, so even the one-line version scrolls while something prints. Builder: session scratchpad `build_printer_status.py` (lost on restart; the boards are the record).
16	
17	**Decided by Kenneth, 2026-11-05:** no collapsed or one-line form. "the best design is to determine if each of those fields need to show. And let the card naturally grow or shrink based on how many fields are being shown." Next step he asked for: each card field's condition to show, per connection type, found the way the status table was (code reads + each printer API's docs, then aggregated).
18	
19	**Field rules** (scratchpad report `printer-card-fields-by-connection.md`, 2026-11-04): each card field has one show-condition, the same for every printer; the connection type only decides if a value exists. **Kenneth, 2026-11-05:** camera "always on as long as the stream is available" (not only while printing or paused); build order "Moonraker, then bambu" (Moonraker activity/job/message/camera in the existing 10 s poll first, then Bambu fields already in MachineObject).
20	
21	**Why:** the card said "Idle" for a Moonraker printer whose Klipper was shut down; root cause was a state field defaulting to Idle that only Bambu sets.
22	
23	**How to apply:** the short-rows board (printer-status-05) is the rejected option; draw cards that grow and shrink by field. Don't build until the field conditions are agreed; see [[kenneth-real-moonraker-raspberrypi-local]].
24	

