1	# When each printer card field shows, by connection type
2	
3	Written 2026-11-04. Every field has one rule for when it shows, and that rule is the same for every printer. The connection type only decides whether the value exists. Today Bambu fills most of the card. Moonraker fills only the connection and the loaded filament. Every other print host fills only the fields the app keeps itself, plus a bare "Connected".
4	
5	Sources: the code at jusprin-newui f8a1476539, and each printer API's docs (links in section 3). The rules in section 1 are a proposal Kenneth has not agreed to. Section 2 says what exists today.
6	
7	## 1. The rule for each field (proposal)
8	
9	The fields are listed top to bottom, as on the boards.
10	
11	| Field | Shows when | Notes |
12	|---|---|---|
13	| Name | Always | |
14	| ⋯ menu | At least one of settings, rename or remove is allowed | Today an unnamed Bambu LAN printer gets none, so its card has no menu |
15	| Camera | Status is Printing or Paused, and the app has a stream for this printer | |
16	| Status word | Always, one of: Printing, Paused, Needs attention, Ready, Connected, Connecting…, Not connected | Comes from the status table already proposed |
17	| Status detail after the dot | Printing: percent, plus "· 2h 14m left" when time left is known. Paused: "at 27%". Otherwise nothing | |
18	| Job name | The printer reports a current job (Printing, Paused, or Needs attention during a job) | |
19	| Progress bar | Same as the job name, and the percent is known | |
20	| Printer's message | Needs attention: always. Paused: when the printer gives a reason. Not connected: always, giving the reason | When the printer sends only a code, show a sentence with the code. When the app never reached the printer, the reason is the app's own words ("octopi.local isn't answering.") |
21	| "Last connected …" | Not connected, and the app knows when it last heard from the printer | Hidden when unknown |
22	| Facts line (connection kind · address · model · nozzle) | Always; each part shows when known | Model and nozzle come from the printer profile for every type, because few printers report them. The address shows for print hosts only |
23	| Loaded filament | The printer reports what is loaded right now | Never a remembered value on a card that is not connected |
24	| History link | At least one print or send record exists | The last print's outcome ("last finished Sun") goes here, only when the printer reports it |
25	| Button | Never set up: "Connect…". Not connected: "Reconnect". Connecting…: none. Otherwise: "Launch monitor" for Bambu, "Open printer window" for a host with a web page | |
26	
27	## 2. Where each value comes from, per connection type
28	
29	Key:
30	- **today**: the card shows it now.
31	- **in app**: the app already receives it but does not send it to the card.
32	- **API**: the printer reports it, and the app needs new reading code.
33	- **calc**: the card has to compute it or look it up.
34	- **—**: not available.
35	- **?**: not confirmed.
36	
37	| Field | Bambu | Moonraker | OctoPrint | PrusaLink | Duet | Flashforge | Elegoo | Creality K | Other hosts* |
38	|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
39	| Activity part of the status | today, partly (paused reads Printing, failed reads Idle) | API | API | API | API | API | API | API | — |
40	| Connection part of the status | today | today | today, since f8a1476539 (any HTTP reply) | same | same | same | same | same | same |
41	| Camera | in app (stream fields; upstream's native player) | API `/server/webcams/list` | API, but the URL is often `localhost` | ? | — | API | API | API | — |
42	| Job name | in app `subtask_name` | API | API | API | API | API | API | API | — |
43	| Percent | today | API | API | API | calc | API | API | API | — |
44	| Time left | today | calc (file estimate minus time printed) | API | API | API | API (freezes while paused) | calc | API | — |
45	| Printer's message | calc (the app's HMS lookup exists) | API, text | API, text | API, text (ATTENTION has none) | API, text | code only | code only | code only | — |
46	| Last connected | in app, in memory only | in app, in memory only | in app, in memory only | same | same | same | same | same | same |
47	| Facts line | in app (connection kind, profile). Nozzle: today | in app (the host type is saved but not sent to the page) | same | same | same | same | same | same | same |
48	| Loaded filament | today (AMS, external spool) | today (`lane_data` or Happy Hare only) | — | — | API, name only, no colour | API, AD5X only | — | API, CFS only | — |
49	| Last print outcome | in app `gcode_state` FINISH/FAILED | API history, kept after the job | — (per file only) | API, until the next job | API, kept after the job | ? | API | — (only inferred) | — |
50	| History | today, prints | today, sends only | today, sends only | same | same | same | same | same | same |
51	
52	*Other hosts are Prusa Connect, Repetier, MKS, ESP3D, FlashAir, AstroBox, SimplyPrint, Obico and 3DPrinterOS. For SimplyPrint and Obico, "answers" means the company's website answered, not the printer.
53	
54	"Last connected" is in memory only for every type, so after a restart the line is hidden until the printer is heard again. Saving the time to disk would fix that.
